---
source: crates/rumps-query/tests/scripts.rs
description: "; Test: type conversions\n; Tests explicit type conversion with AS and string interpolation\n\n; === Explicit Type Conversion with AS ===\n\n; Addition with explicit conversion to Float\nLET a = (10 AS Float) + 3.5\nWRITE a\n; Expected: 13.5 (Float)\n\nLET b = 3.5 + (10 AS Float)\nWRITE b\n; Expected: 13.5 (Float)\n\n; Subtraction with explicit conversion\nLET c = (10 AS Float) - 2.5\nWRITE c\n; Expected: 7.5 (Float)\n\nLET d = 10.5 - (3 AS Float)\nWRITE d\n; Expected: 7.5 (Float)\n\n; Multiplication with explicit conversion\nLET e = (5 AS Float) * 2.5\nWRITE e\n; Expected: 12.5 (Float)\n\nLET f = 2.5 * (4 AS Float)\nWRITE f\n; Expected: 10.0 (Float)\n\n; Division (requires Float operands)\nLET g = (10 AS Float) / 4.0\nWRITE g\n; Expected: 2.5 (Float)\n\nLET h = 10.0 / (4 AS Float)\nWRITE h\n; Expected: 2.5 (Float)\n\n; Float division\nLET i = 10.0 / 5.0\nWRITE i\n; Expected: 2.0 (Float)\n\n; Floor division (same-type operands)\nLET j = 10.0 // 3.0\nWRITE j\n; Expected: 3.0 (Float)\n\nLET k = 10 // 3\nWRITE k\n; Expected: 3 (Int)\n\n; Modulo (same-type operands)\nLET l = 10.0 % 3.5\nWRITE l\n; Expected: 3.0 (Float; 10.0 % 3.5 = 3.0)\n\nLET m = 10.5 % 3.0\nWRITE m\n; Expected: 1.5 (Float; 10.5 % 3.0 = 1.5)\n\n; === String Conversion (via interpolation) ===\n\n; Int to string\nWRITE \"Number: {42}\"\n; Expected: Number: 42\n\n; Float to string\nWRITE \"Pi: {3.14159}\"\n; Expected: Pi: 3.14159\n\n; Bool to string\nWRITE \"Flag: {TRUE}\"\n; Expected: Flag: true\n\nWRITE \"Flag: {FALSE}\"\n; Expected: Flag: false\n\n; === Same-type Numeric Comparison ===\n\nWRITE 5 == 5\n; Expected: true\n\nWRITE 5.0 == 5.0\n; Expected: true\n\nWRITE 10 < 11\n; Expected: true\n\nWRITE 10.5 > 10.0\n; Expected: true\n\nWRITE 3 >= 3\n; Expected: true\n\nWRITE 3.0 <= 3.0\n; Expected: true\n\nWRITE \"Type conversion test complete\"\n"
---
